---
// "Hand it to your coding agent": one prompt that works whether or not an A2G SDK exists for the game's engine.
const origin = Astro.site!;
const url = (path: string) => new URL(path, origin).href;
const prompt = `Read ${url('/llms-full.txt')}, the Agent2Game (A2G) protocol 0.1. Then integrate A2G into this game.

1. Identify the engine and language. If an A2G SDK exists for it (see Implementations), use it.
2. If there is no SDK, write a small client in the game's language that follows the specification and the rules in ${url('/guides/integrate/#no-sdk-for-your-engine')}: keep it game-agnostic and separate from game code; never block a frame on the network; validate every decision (epoch, legal_actions, ttl_ms); fall back to the game's existing AI on any error, timeout or FALLBACK; send reports with decision_id and telemetry about once per second; validate messages in tests against ${url('/schema/0.1/a2g.schema.json')}.
3. Propose a manifest from the game's real entities: what each can observe and the actions it already has. Prefer enums and fractions; never include personal data.
4. Write the adapter (observe, legal_actions, execute) and hook the entities so the original AI stays the default and the fallback.
5. Never put provider API keys in the game. Show me the plan and the manifest before changing existing game logic.`;
---

<section class="agent-prompt not-content" aria-labelledby="agent-title">
	<div class="head">
		<div>
			<h2 id="agent-title">Hand it to your coding agent</h2>
			<p>Paste this into Claude Code, Codex or Cursor in your game's project. It uses an SDK when your engine has one and writes a client by the rules when it does not.</p>
		</div>
		<button type="button" class="copy" data-copy={prompt}>Copy prompt</button>
	</div>
	<div class="prompt" data-open="false">
		<pre>{prompt}</pre>
	</div>
	<button type="button" class="more" aria-expanded="false">Show all</button>
</section>

<script>
	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.agent-prompt')) {
		const copy = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy')!;
		const box = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.prompt')!;
		const more = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.more')!;
		copy.addEventListener('click', async () => {
			try {
				await navigator.clipboard.writeText(copy.dataset.copy ?? '');
				copy.textContent = 'Copied';
			} catch {
				// Clipboard blocked (permissions, insecure context): open and select the prompt so ⌘C / Ctrl+C works.
				box.dataset.open = 'true';
				more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
				getSelection()?.selectAllChildren(box.querySelector('pre')!);
				copy.textContent = 'Press ⌘C';
			}
			setTimeout(() => (copy.textContent = 'Copy prompt'), 2000);
		});
		more.addEventListener('click', () => {
			const open = box.dataset.open !== 'true';
			box.dataset.open = String(open);
			more.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(open));
			more.textContent = open ? 'Show less' : 'Show all';
		});
	}
</script>

<style>
	.agent-prompt {
		margin: 1rem 0 3rem;
		padding: 1.25rem;
		border-radius: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	.head {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-items: flex-start;
		justify-content: space-between;
	}
	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	.head p {
		margin: 0.3rem 0 0;
		max-width: 44rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.copy,
	.more {
		font: inherit;
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.copy {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
		border: 0;
		border-radius: 0.45rem;
		background: var(--a2g-ai);
		color: #07150f;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.copy:focus-visible,
	.more:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--sl-color-accent);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.prompt {
		position: relative;
		margin-top: 1rem;
		border-radius: 0.5rem;
		background: var(--sl-color-black);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
	}
	pre {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
		max-height: 7.5rem;
		overflow: hidden;
		font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		white-space: pre-wrap;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
		mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 55%, transparent);
	}
	.prompt[data-open='true'] pre {
		max-height: none;
		mask-image: none;
	}
	.more {
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		padding: 0;
		border: 0;
		background: none;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
	}
	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.head {
			flex-direction: column;
		}
	}
</style>
